Make the colour-naming import optional.

Upstream pin: VLA-3D @ a0c023c9662bd875f0b3aeff4ff60adc1991e449

generate_scene_info.py imports colors.py at module scope, and colors.py imports a private module
of the webcolors package (webcolors._definitions) to name object colours for the language
generator. Nothing on the relation path uses it: the relate_* functions take boxes and classes.
This lets the module import without webcolors rather than adding a dependency, pinned to a
private module path, for code we never call.

Without it: importing the relation functions fails with ModuleNotFoundError: webcolors.

